# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except the example, which holds no secrets and is the only record of which
# variables a working build needs. It being ignored is how the RevenueCat keys
# went missing: the native app shipped with no way to take a payment, and
# nothing in the repository said a key was expected.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Capacitor native projects (committed) — but not their generated/local-only build output
android/.gradle
android/build
android/app/build
android/local.properties
android/.idea
android/**/*.iml
ios/App/build
# Capacitor 8 builds through SPM, so xcodebuild drops its DerivedData here
# rather than in ios/App/build — untracked noise on every simulator build.
ios/App/CapApp-SPM/build
ios/App/Pods
ios/App/App.xcworkspace/xcuserdata
ios/App/App.xcodeproj/xcuserdata
ios/App/App.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcuserdata
ios/DerivedData

# claude-flow agent runtime state — daemon pid/logs, metrics, neural stats and
# headless audit transcripts. Machine-local and regenerated on every run, so it
# only ever produces conflicts and noise in diffs. The headless audit logs also
# capture prompt and result text, which does not belong in a shared repo.
.claude-flow/

# The UAT personas' report, written by an afterAll hook in tests/uat and read
# back by scripts/check-uat-report.mjs. Committed until 22 Sep 2026, which was
# the problem that script exists to describe: a milestone was checked by
# grepping this file, so it "stayed green for as long as nobody re-ran the
# bots" — a file's memory of a result rather than the result. The script now
# runs the suite and reads what THAT run wrote, with a freshness check, so
# nothing needs the committed copy. Tracked, it only ever arrived as noise in
# unrelated diffs.
docs/pre-launch/uat-bot-report.md

# Supabase CLI link state, written by `supabase link`. Machine-local, and
# `pooler-url` is a database connection string — the one file in this repo that
# would be worst to commit. It was untracked but not ignored, which is one
# `git add -A` away from being in the history, and that is exactly how the UAT
# report got swept into an unrelated commit on 22 Sep.
supabase/.temp/
